repro/b2-refl-usage.wiz:9:1: error: kernel rejected bad: cannot project p.1: a projection needs an unrestricted pair (it keeps one component and drops the other), but this one uses p, which has quantity 0; this is a field of a structure, and a structure can't be held at a quantity other than ω yet (it has no destructuring form); use a tuple `A × B` instead, taken apart with `let 0 (x, y) := …`
